  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/34f00120-c640-45e0-b31a-b63327016d5d.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 173px;\"/></p><p>Linear momentum will be conserved, therefore</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>≅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Again from energy conservation, we get height achieved, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.2</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.</p>",
